WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.818
Once you have real history, you need to manage it.

2
00:00:01.818 --> 00:00:06.000
Folders, snapshots, branching, and compaction — the tools for a chat list that has grown past a handful of entries.

3
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:14.222
Right-click any chat: pin it, rename it or leave auto-title running, move it to a folder, duplicate it, export as Markdown or JSON, or delete it.

4
00:00:14.222 --> 00:00:17.000
Delete has no undo — that is the one to pause on.

5
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:21.618
Before a risky tool-using task — one that edits files or runs commands — take a snapshot.

6
00:00:21.618 --> 00:00:23.123
If it goes wrong, restore it.

7
00:00:23.123 --> 00:00:28.000
The chat keeps its identity through a restore; it is the same chat rolled back, not a new one.

8
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.103
Branch and edit look similar but do different jobs.

9
00:00:30.103 --> 00:00:35.835
Branch from a message forks a new chat and leaves the original untouched — good for exploring an alternative without losing the first path.

10
00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:40.000
Edit a message changes history in place, in the same chat — good when you just got the wording wrong.

11
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.521
Compact shows a banner and folds older turns down to a summary, keeping recent messages verbatim.

12
00:00:44.521 --> 00:00:51.000
Turn on auto-compact with a threshold and it happens on its own once a chat crosses a length you set, instead of waiting for you to notice.

13
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:55.181
Gotcha: compaction loses detail on purpose — that is the whole mechanism, not a bug.

14
00:00:55.181 --> 00:01:02.000
Anything you will want verbatim later belongs in an export or in memory before it gets folded, not left to survive compaction on its own.

15
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:02.896
Managing chats is free.

16
00:01:02.896 --> 00:01:03.675
Running them is not.

17
00:01:03.675 --> 00:01:08.000
Next we make the cost picture concrete — where the money actually goes, and the handful of levers that move it.

